{
  "about": [
    "chat filter rules: the per-rule hide / highlight engine (the setting chatFilterRules), one file for every app.",
    "each case is a list of raw rules as the setting stores them, one chat line, the channel tab the line is in, and the verdict the rules give it.",
    "rules are run in order the way the engine does: rules for every channel first, then the channel's own; the first hide wins outright, otherwise the first highlight gives the colour and sound.",
    "msg: text, user (a youtube name arrives as @handle), badges (twitch/kick: 'set/ver,set/ver'; youtube: a list of names), platform, isFirstMsg, isAction, bits, replyTo ({user} or null).",
    "a msg field left out is: user alice, badges none, platform twitch, isFirstMsg false, isAction false, bits 0, replyTo null. channel '' means no channel tab.",
    "want: hide; color = the highlight's colour (a hex colour or null: an app that draws from a palette checks only that there is one); notify; sound = a sound name or 'custom' or null; soundVolume = 0 to 100 or null (follow the shared volume).",
    "a rule that cannot be compiled (empty value, unknown action or type, a malformed expression) is dropped and the others still run.",
    "channel ids are lowercase names; the ext compares a rule's channel to the tab's exactly, an app may compare without regard to case, so no case here depends on it.",
    "not here, on purpose: the ext's regex denylist (a nested-quantifier or alternation pattern is read as plain text there; a linear-time regex engine needs none) and its 4 ms head-first timing, which are not deterministic.",
    "a runner that meets a field or a verdict it does not know must fail, never skip."
  ],
